	(text "v1 TODO\n\n[x] silk markings for usb testpoints\n[x] more ESD diodes on FFC\n[x] ffc socket under TPM for idk LoRa addon (interferes with TPM EP =( )\n[x] markings for hardware switches!\n[x] fix iovcc when powered from vsys\n[x] rename to just zero\n[x] fix tpm i2c\n[x] rewire for esp32-c5\n[x] retune sdio length\n[x] picoprobe-compatible UART 3-pin JST-SH\n[x] extra button(s) for button-on-the-bottom pi zero format boards\n[x] i2c touch fallback on the 40-pin display conn (allows for FFC adapters if someone is wild enough to design one)\n[x] route neopixel output to uhhhhh??? idk lol\n[x] default state pulls on display pins? (only CS called for)\n[x] adjust esp32 qwiic position (cuz of the PWM chip)\n[x] fox\n[x] some sort of connectors for easier touchpad/etc i2c0/i2c1 connectivity?\n[x] conn for cool display touch\n[x] touch connector?\n[x] hall sensor\n[x] 2.2k pulldown on mic (i forgor) (used 2k)\n[x] temp sensors on i2c!\n[x] current sensor for CPU consumption!\n[x] extra USB tap\n[x] center the expansion conn\n[x] gpio neopixel driver jumper\n[x] silk squares on gnd on exp conn for reference\n[x] uart tx/rx arrows on silk to mark exp connector and qwiic polarity in a more immediately visible way\n[x] switch ec int to a npxl-capable pin\n[x] standalone npxl control from ec int\n[x] pin 1 markers everywhere\n  [x] meowpixels\n  [x] TVS diode\n[x] override for the fusb302!!! (for radxa zero)\n  [x] inline resistor for gpio\n[x] analog audio header markings\n[x] buttons on the front (for ZPUI)\n  [x] that one tiny 5-way keypad\n  [x] or one of those tiney joysticks\n  [x] TODO go through my newly acquired funny switches trove, lmfao\n[x] put sdio pullups after the sdio series resistors\n[x] radxa a7z pcie port cutout\n[x] move zero footprint towards outside\n[x] display backlight connector\n[x] spi pin header silk\n[x] qwiic footprint for USB uplink\n[x] pullup for the modem power pgood?\n[x] 480x320 ILI9488 3.5\"/4.0\" SPI display\n[x] spi series resistors\n[x] display-TPM CS switch flip\n[x] testpoints for other SPI displays (UPD a whole header, even!)\n[x] extend solderable display pads\n[x] optional i2c pullups on pi zero i2c\n[x] eeprom i2c disconnectable!\n[x] i2c driver for backlight\n  [x] disconnect screen_bl from gpio expander\n  [x] flashlight\n  [n] check other such drivers I saw\n  [n] route extra LEDs to the free pins?\n[x] more usb port pads (for easier data line tapping on next versions)\n[x] pi zero numbering warning\n[x] serial number field\n[x] sdio pullups\n[x] fusb fuse\n[x] route sbc gpios to bottom ffc header for expansion yippie\n[x] some sorta eeprom that's readable/writable by the ec?? id eeprom reading/writing would be funny\n[x] thicken sim_vdd track\n[x] expose a7682e uart\n[x] 5V for display backlight to actual 5V\n[x] reposition neopixels to accommodate radxa under-board microsd slots (make them vertical, move closer to exp)\n[x] dual HAT EEPROM! (switch ADDR by IO_MUX_SEL)\n  [n] with override from an EC GPIO? maybe? idk it shouldn't be needed\n[n] move esp switch to other side of esp?\n	[n] does that still allow a standoff?\n[n] antenna cable slot\n[n] rotate the sy at the qwiic a lil (sadly can't)\n[n] re-silk jumpers\n[n] esp32 non-soldered pads exposed?\n[n] other adjustments, maybe testpoints? for boards with fucked up 40-pin conns (i.e. radxa zero v1.5)\n[n] extra 3.3V reg for when the on-CPU one fucks up? only really useful for the ESP32-C6 and the expansion port.\\\n[n] add something in the area above the two hardware switches (LEDs?)\n[n] play out the \"palmtop powered from top board usbc\" scenario\n[n] useful names for testpoints/jumpers\n[n] USB-serial\n[?] testpoints? for cpu platform bringup. maybe more for the universal board.\n[?] unite the usb mux gpios into one(?)\n[?] fix the gpio (?)\n[?] diode from ec_present for autoboot?\n[?] bottom: boot button footprint? WITH DIODE"
